From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@docker01.fra.askei.net>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(qwen4): CPU-offload correctness, breakable graphs,
 mmap PLE table

Port the accepted 3090 correctness, host-fix, graph-output and PLE changes
onto upstream main b02e16a895 (model support 52fecfdf). Ported from the
frozen serving tree (docs/logs/raw/migration_3090_2026-09-16).

- offloader: offload only streamed expert params under
  SGLANG_MOE_EXPERT_STREAM, skip the forward hook when every offloaded param
  is a streamed expert, exclude streamed params from the rebuilt state_dict,
  pass tie_weights=False to functional_call (tied linear_attn A_log), and
  keep a hard reference to the pinned host storage.
- GemmaRMSNorm: keep gemma_weight on the parameter's device (non-persistent
  buffer is not moved by --cpu-offload-gb); derive it per forward.
- Qwen3_5/RadixLinearAttention: pass the nn.Conv1d module and derive the 2D
  view on each access so a stale view cannot point at replaced param.data.
- QSA indexer: size the rotary cos/sin cache to the server context length
  once instead of positions.max().item() per layer.
- Breakable graph backend: teach the structure helpers the
  LogitsProcessorOutput dataclass (capture/replay).
- Qwen4-Exp: mmap PLE table on meta device, parallel pread with a bounded
  recent-row cache and MADV_RANDOM/POSIX_FADV_RANDOM, packed_modules_mapping
  propagation, eager graph break for the PLE lookup, and register
  Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration for language-model-only.

The already-upstream qwen_sparse_attention alias is not re-added. Optional
NGRAM speculation, INT2/streaming, placement/elastic/lazy KV, quantized QSA,
PP and RC/RB follow in later commits.
